// budget reservation, because a run that discovers it is over its ceiling after spending is not a
// ceiling: the SKU bills per returned contact, so the worst case is the whole requested limit.
//
// Both decisions live HERE rather than in the node that builds the request bodies, and that is the
// fix for a real defect. They used to sit in Build Domain Editor Calls, which emitted an item for
// every prospect and marked the skipped ones with a flag instead of a request body. Those items
// still flowed into the HTTP node, which POSTed an empty body and got back
// `invalid_input: missing property 'domain'`. Measured on one run: 43 of 61 calls to this SKU were
// that 400. They cost nothing, but they were pure noise in the log and the prospects behind them
// were reported as "no named editor is published", which is a different thing from "we never
// asked". Deciding here means the existing false branch carries them to the merge untouched.
